question:
Points $A$, $B$, $C$ and $D$ are midpoints of the sides of the larger square.  If the larger square has area 60, what is the area of the smaller square? [asy]
pair a=(0,1),b=(1,0),c=(0,-1),d=(-1,0);
draw((-1,-1)--(-1,1)--(1,1)--(1,-1)--cycle);
draw(a--b--c--d--cycle);
label("$A$", a, N);
label("$B$", b, E);
label("$C$", c, S);
label("$D$", d, W);
[/asy]

What is the least number of colors needed to shade the tessellation shown, such that no two tiles sharing a side are the same color?

[asy]
draw((-8,-2)--(8,-2));
draw((-8,2)--(8,2));
draw((-8,6)--(8,6));
draw((-8,10)--(8,10));
draw((-8,14)--(8,14));
path a=(-8,14)--(-6.5,12)--(-10,8)--(-6.5,4)--(-10,0)--(-8,-2);
draw(a);
draw(shift((4,0))*a);
draw(shift((8,0))*a);
draw(shift((12,0))*a);
draw(shift((16,0))*a);
[/asy]

In right triangle $ABC$, $M$ and $N$ are midpoints of legs $\overline{AB}$ and $\overline{BC}$, respectively. Leg $\overline{AB}$ is 6 units long, and leg $\overline{BC}$ is 8 units long. How many square units are in the area of $\triangle APC$? [asy]
draw((0,0)--(8,0)--(0,6)--cycle);
draw((4,0)--(0,6));
draw((0,3)--(8,0));
label("$A$",(0,6),NW); label("$B$",(0,0),SW); label("$C$",(8,0),SE); label("$M$",(0,3),W); label("$N$",(4,0),S); label("$P$",(8/3,2),SW);
[/asy]
